Altered ArmorPaint color-layer blur adaptation in Dome Sculpt.

Source: https://github.com/armory3d/armorpaint
Commit: 629f8e77b3f19d533c60a1baa4fe9d4db9ee1163
Original: paint/sources/render/make_blur.c, retained unchanged at
experiments/armorpaint-blur/vendor/make_blur.c, with the complete zlib/libpng
license at experiments/armorpaint-blur/vendor/LICENSE.armorpaint.

The build copies the exact get_blur_tool_weight function offline into the build
directory. src/paint-blur-gpu.cpp is an ALTERED texture-space cross-filter
adaptation. It adds typed common/PBR colors, independent authored alpha and
coverage, sRGB conversion, per-chart normalization, independent mask gating,
dirty tiles/halos and private EGL/PBO/fence ownership. It does not import the
upstream frontend, engine, project/history format, packed normal/material roles
or complete painting/material/baking workflow.

Native host, transaction/history integration and independent tests are
GPL-3.0-or-later. The native EGL helper retains its separate MIT notice in
third_party/openbrush/LICENSE.native-graphics and its documented local changes.
This adaptation is not the upstream ArmorPaint application. Preserve the
upstream license and attribution when distributing the derived application.
